{"id":"a9","level":2,"levelName":"Ulpan Alef","n":9,"of":10,"title":"What's happening now","titleHe":"זְמַן הֹוֶה","goal":"Use the present tense — four forms, no persons.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"The Hebrew present has only four forms, and they change for gender and number rather than for person. אֲנִי כּוֹתֵב, אַתָּה כּוֹתֵב and הוּא כּוֹתֵב are all the same word — the pronoun does the rest."},{"type":"binyan","he":"פָּעַל","en":"pa'al (kal)","note":"The plain, basic verb — the one most everyday actions use.","verb":{"root":"כ־ת־ב","inf":"לִכְתֹּב","en":"to write"},"tense":"present","rows":[{"label":"masculine singular","he":"","form":"כּוֹתֵב"},{"label":"feminine singular","he":"","form":"כּוֹתֶבֶת"},{"label":"masculine plural","he":"","form":"כּוֹתְבִים"},{"label":"feminine plural","he":"","form":"כּוֹתְבוֹת"}]},{"type":"text","body":"It covers both English presents at once: אֲנִי קוֹרֵא is I read and I am reading."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"אֲנִי לוֹמֵד עִבְרִית.","en":"I'm learning Hebrew."},{"he":"הִיא גָּרָה בָּעִיר.","en":"She lives in the city."},{"he":"הֵם אוֹכְלִים בַּבַּיִת.","en":"They're eating at home."}]}],"vocab":[{"he":"לוֹמֵד","en":"learns, studies","translit":"lomed"},{"he":"כּוֹתֵב","en":"writes","translit":"kotev"},{"he":"קוֹרֵא","en":"reads","translit":"kore"},{"he":"אוֹכֵל","en":"eats","translit":"ochel"},{"he":"הוֹלֵךְ","en":"goes, walks","translit":"holech"},{"he":"יוֹשֵׁב","en":"sits","translit":"yoshev"},{"he":"גָּר","en":"lives, resides","translit":"gar"},{"he":"רוֹצֶה","en":"wants","translit":"rotse"},{"he":"אוֹהֵב","en":"loves, likes","translit":"ohev"},{"he":"עִבְרִית","en":"Hebrew","translit":"ivrit"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["his name","reading, a call","teacher (m.)","learns, studies"],"correct":3,"prompt":"לוֹמֵד","translit":"lomed"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["people, men","end","writes","son"],"correct":2,"prompt":"כּוֹתֵב","translit":"kotev"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["decides","money","reads","development"],"correct":2,"prompt":"קוֹרֵא","translit":"kore"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["beginning","maybe","eats","dog"],"correct":2,"prompt":"אוֹכֵל","translit":"ochel"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["goes, walks","in, at","comes","before, not yet"],"correct":0,"prompt":"הוֹלֵךְ","translit":"holech"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["houses","sits","hello, peace","to her"],"correct":1,"prompt":"יוֹשֵׁב","translit":"yoshev"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["lives, resides","with me","which","at all, in general"],"correct":0,"prompt":"גָּר","translit":"gar"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “eats”?","options":["תֵּן","אוֹכֵל","מַכִּיר","אוֹתוֹ"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["קוֹרֵא","אוֹהֵב","עִבְרִית","יוֹשֵׁב"],"correct":1,"say":"אוֹהֵב","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"write — masculine plural, present","options":["כּוֹתֶבֶת","כּוֹתְבוֹת","כּוֹתֵב","כּוֹתְבִים"],"correct":3,"he":true,"why":"פָּעַל, present: masculine plural is כּוֹתְבִים."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “reads”?","options":["לְ","קוֹרֵא","בִּכְלָל","לָמָּה"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["הוֹלֵךְ","goes, walks"],["לוֹמֵד","learns, studies"],["גָּר","lives, resides"],["רוֹצֶה","wants"],["יוֹשֵׁב","sits"]]},{"type":"read","he":"רוֹצֶה","translit":"rotse","en":"wants"},{"type":"choice","q":"write — feminine singular, present","options":["כּוֹתְבִים","כּוֹתֶבֶת","כּוֹתְבוֹת","כּוֹתֵב"],"correct":1,"he":true,"why":"פָּעַל, present: feminine singular is כּוֹתֶבֶת."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “sits”?","options":["מַכִּיר","אֵין","יוֹשֵׁב","מְקַבֵּל"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"write — feminine plural, present","options":["כּוֹתֶבֶת","כּוֹתְבוֹת","כּוֹתֵב","כּוֹתְבִים"],"correct":1,"he":true,"why":"פָּעַל, present: feminine plural is כּוֹתְבוֹת."}]}